
WrapDL is a small C library that wraps dynamic linker.

On Linux, macOS, and Windows it uses the normal system loader (dlopen,
LoadLibrary, etc.) with one simple API.

On Android it adds extra behavior from xDL-style code: better symbol lookup
on already-loaded libraries, and optional linker namespace bypass for
loading libs outside the app sandbox.

Public header: include/wrapdl.h

Build:
  cmake -B build
  cmake --build build

Or:
  make build
  make linux-test

Android sample app: tests/android/wrapdltest

